Notebook[{
Cell["Lesson 14 - Adimensional", "Title",ExpressionUUID->"3e0341b3-a386-4b09-ade4-bee6b474f0bc"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Physics step.",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 " Turn the dimensionful equations ",
 StyleBox["\[PartialD]",
  FontFamily->"Noto Sans"],
 "s(comb) = ",
 StyleBox["\[Integral]",
  FontFamily->"Noto Sans"],
 "d",
 StyleBox["\:1d48",
  FontFamily->"Noto Sans"],
 "q/(2",
 StyleBox["\[Pi]",
  FontFamily->"Noto Sans"],
 ")",
 StyleBox["\:1d48",
  FontFamily->"Noto Sans"],
 " I(q) into dimensionless ",
 StyleBox["\[Beta]",
  FontFamily->"Noto Sans"],
 " functions. Each state coupling c becomes ",
 StyleBox["\:0109",
  FontFamily->"Noto Sans"],
 " = c/[c], with"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"30ca9658-aa4c-4d41-8478-7c9913fbd799"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["\[PartialD]",
  FontFamily->"Noto Sans"],
 "s ",
 StyleBox["\:0109",
  FontFamily->"Noto Sans"],
 " = BetaL + ",
 StyleBox["\[Integral]",
  FontFamily->"Noto Sans"],
 "daq LoopMeasure(d, aq) BetaNL,  LoopMeasure = S_d aq^{d",
 StyleBox["\[Minus]",
  FontFamily->"Noto Sans"],
 "1}/(2",
 StyleBox["\[Pi]",
  FontFamily->"Noto Sans"],
 ")^d,"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"5de4edbd-968c-4205-825f-6869185ccb27"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "where BetaL is the local part (canonical scaling and Leibniz terms, not \
integrated) and BetaNL the loop integrand in the dimensionless momentum aq = \
q/k. The reference couplings do not get a ",
 StyleBox["\[Beta]",
  FontFamily->"Noto Sans"],
 ": their running gives a linear system for the anomalous dimensions ",
 StyleBox["\[Eta]",
  FontFamily->"Noto Sans"],
 ". The module proves that nothing depends on k or on the references any more."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"ea8992e0-764a-4f7a-b6ff-9ad120bbf7ed"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Stage.",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 " Input: the Equations stage (lesson 11) and the Dimensions stage (lesson \
13), from the same ansatz. Output: the ",
 StyleBox["\"Adimensional\"",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro",
  FontColor->RGBColor[0.6, 0.12, 0.1],
  Background->GrayLevel[0.92]],
 " stage, the input of the Julia export."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"3069a962-faa0-4027-a526-897774112325"],

Cell["\<\
Get[\"~/Physics/Sources/FRGscalarMSR/FRGscalarMSR.wl\"];
Get[FileNameJoin[{$FRGRoot, \"lessons\", \"LessonSetup.wl\"}]];
equations = lessonUpTo[\"Equations\"];
dims = Block[{Print}, DeriveDimensions[kpzAnsatz, \"References\" -> {nuk -> \
\"nu\", Dk -> \"D\"}, \"Scale\" -> k]];\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"b9ee9aa0-675c-4908-9311-63d38c0032c8"],

Cell["1. Using it", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"0115318d-9ce6-4553-b7b2-f172cab05141"],

Cell["adim = AdimensionalEquations[equations, dims];", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"ecee7a0c-54b1-4506-be1c-f833f36d4ca4"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "KPZ has one state coupling, ",
